findings.body:
Returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: origin ?? "*"` together with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: "true"`. Per the CORS spec, `*` (or a reflected arbitrary origin) may not be used with credentials; browsers will refuse or expose the response insecurely. Any mobile webview or attacker-controlled origin can now send authenticated requests.

```suggestion
  if (!origin || !isAllowedOrigin(origin)) {
    return {};
  }
  return {
    "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin,
    "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials": "true",
    Vary: "Origin",
  };
```
